# Iterate: a drawing is kept and improved in place. Each change says only what changes (the same id again, a move, a new part);
# everything else stays exactly where it was, so a follow-up costs a few lines and the picture never starts over.

look paper
scene boat figure lines=2
line sea 0,70 160,70 thick=1
poly hull 50,60 110,60 100,72 60,72 fill=ink
rect mast 78,26 2x34 fill=ink
say | A first draft of a boat.
wait 2
poly sail 80,28 80,56 104,56 fill=accent
say | Ask for a sail and only the sail arrives.
wait 2
poly sail 80,22 80,56 116,56 fill=accent
say | Make it bigger: the same sail, said again with new corners.
wait 2
circle sun 132,20 8 fill=alt stroke=none
poly flag 82,26 82,18 92,22 fill=alt
say label near=flag:above | flag
say | A sun and a flag more. Nothing before them was redrawn.
wait 2
move hull 70,66 over=1.5s
move mast 98,40 over=1.5s
move sail 100,40 over=1.5s
move flag 100,24 over=1.5s
say | And the boat sets off. /undo puts the drawing back as it was before the last change.
wait 2
